--------------------------------------------------------------------------------
WHAT SHIPPED
--------------------------------------------------------------------------------
A complete, HIG-native SwiftUI RbacMatrixPage at web parity: a pure @Observable
state holder (ADR-004 — no networking in the view) over an injectable
RbacMatrixDataSource seam whose value types mirror the web RbacRole /
RbacPermission / RbacMatrixSessionResponse / RbacUpsertCell 1:1 (production binds
the KMP RBAC endpoints GET/PUT /admin/rbac/matrix through the seam). The page is
the provider-agnostic "who can do what" admin matrix: columns = proxy-group roles,
rows = the permission catalog grouped by category, cells = allow (✓) / deny (–).

Read-only by default; the Edit toggle flips cells into checkboxes and Save diffs
the draft against the snapshot and PUTs only the changed cells (sudo-gated upstream
→ the reauth dialog pops transparently). One query drives the page, so its four
data states are switched in place — never a blank region. All three web GlassPanels
are reproduced:

  GlassPanel1 — the AUTH_MODE_OPEN forward-auth notice (web `rbac-open-mode`):
    explains the FORWARD_AUTH_HEADER / TESLASYNC_RBAC_GROUPS_HEADER requirement
    instead of a 401/501 toast loop. (RbacMatrixPage.swift > openModePanel)
  GlassPanel2 — the summary bar (web `rbac-summary`): my-roles + effective-permission
    pills + the optional groups-header name, and the read-only⇄edit controls
    (Edit, or Cancel + Save with the live dirty-cell count).
    (RbacMatrixPage.Summary.swift > RbacSummaryPanel)
  GlassPanel3 — the role×permission grid (web `MatrixGrid`): category-grouped rows,
    ✓/– read glyphs ⇄ ≥44pt edit checkboxes, adaptive (a horizontally-scrollable
    columnar Grid on macOS/iPad regular, per-permission cards on compact iPhone).
    (RbacMatrixPage.Grid.swift > RbacMatrixGridPanel + RbacMatrixCell)

The pure web matrix algebra was ported 1:1 and unit-tested: snapshotToDraft (deep
copy), diffMatrices (changed cells, missing-as-false, deterministic order),
isRbacOpenMode (envelope narrowing), permsByCategory + orderedCategories
(category grouping). Save-failure keeps edit mode + shows the API code (web
`submitError`); load-failure shows the code or the generic copy + Retry.

Files (all new unless noted):
  Sources/Features/Admin/RbacMatrixModels.swift            (value types/states/seam/pure logic)
  Sources/Features/Admin/RbacMatrixPageModel.swift         (@Observable model)
  Sources/Features/Admin/RbacMatrixPageModel.Sample.swift  (actor seed source)
  Sources/Features/Admin/RbacMatrixPage.swift              (chrome + 4 states + GlassPanel1)
  Sources/Features/Admin/RbacMatrixPage.Summary.swift      (GlassPanel2 + pills)
  Sources/Features/Admin/RbacMatrixPage.Grid.swift         (GlassPanel3 + cell)
  Sources/Features/Admin/RbacMatrixRouteRegistration.swift (.rbacMatrix route)
  Tests/Unit/Features/Admin/RbacMatrixPageModelTests.swift (state-machine + matrix-algebra tests)
  Sources/App/AppRoute.swift          (MOD: +.rbacMatrix case / pathSegment / icon / System group)
  Sources/App/AppRouteParser.swift    (MOD: +"/admin/rbac" + "/admin/rbac-matrix" aliases)
  Sources/TeslaSyncApp.swift          (MOD: wire RbacMatrixRouteRegistration; flattened the
                                       routeHosts builder into `routeHostRegistry` so adding a
                                       registration never breaches the line-length budget)
  Localization/Localizable.xcstrings  (MOD: +29 bare keys: 23 required rbac.* + 5 rbac.category.* + route.rbacMatrix)
  apps/parity/apple-ledger.json       (MOD: +2 rows page:admin/RbacMatrix 30/30 macos+ios)

Navigation reconciliation: the web page is `(unrouted)` (reached via the admin nav
tree), so it resolves to a dedicated .rbacMatrix route (pathSegment "rbac-matrix",
System sidebar group) via AppRouteParser "/admin/rbac" + "/admin/rbac-matrix"
aliases — mirroring the sibling .featureFlags (/admin/flags) pattern — reachable +
deep-linkable without displacing other admin pages. The generated
TeslaSync.xcodeproj + the built Frameworks/Shared.xcframework are git-ignored.

